      "refersTo": "side-panel",
      "description": "The single home for forms, with actions pinned at the bottom.",
      "html": "<aside class=\"ds-panel\"><header><h2>Invite someone</h2></header><div class=\"ds-body\">Fields scroll here.</div><footer><button class=\"ds-cancel\">Done</button><button class=\"ds-send\">Send invitation</button></footer></aside>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{display:flex;flex-direction:column;width:320px;height:300px;background:var(--surface);color:var(--text);border-left:1px solid var(--border);box-shadow:0 24px 64px -16px rgb(0 0 0 / .14),0 4px 12px rgb(0 0 0 / .04);font:400 13.5px 'Roboto Flex',system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-panel header{padding:14px 24px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);}.ds-panel h2{margin:0;font:400 22px/1.25 'Frank Ruhl Libre',Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.015em;}.ds-body{flex:1;padding:20px 24px;color:var(--muted);}.ds-panel footer{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;gap:8px;padding:12px 24px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);}.ds-panel button{height:36px;padding:0 14px;border-radius:8px;font:500 13.5px 'Roboto Flex',system-ui,sans-serif;cursor:pointer;}.ds-cancel{background:var(--surface);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--border);}.ds-send{background:var(--ink);color:var(--on-ink);border:0;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Drafting Table",
    "overview": "The interface disappears into the work. Pages are drawn in black ink on faint graph paper, with one serif title to say where you are. Color appears once per view, where it means something.\n\nThe app is an Operate surface: people come to finish a task, often between other jobs and sometimes on a phone. Density is compact and text is small but high in contrast, so a page holds a lot without feeling crowded. The serif appears only in titles and headline figures. Everything a person reads while working is in the sans.\n\nThis is also a boilerplate that forks and Partners re-skin, so the system's character lives in ink, line and spacing. The brand arrives through the accent tokens and the logo, and a page must still look finished when that accent is someone else's blue.\n\n- Near-monochrome ink and neutrals, with a single replaceable accent.\n- Serif titles over a compact sans working layer.\n- A faint graph-paper grid and brand glow that fade out down the page.\n- Cards rest on soft shadows, and hairlines divide what is inside them.\n- Every form opens in one side panel.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-monochrome ink and neutrals, with a single replaceable accent.",
      "Serif titles over a compact sans working layer.",
      "A faint graph-paper grid and brand glow that fade out down the page.",
      "Cards rest on soft shadows, and hairlines divide what is inside them.",
      "Every form opens in one side panel."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Highlighter Rule",
        "body": "The accent appears at most once or twice in a view, and only where it means something. Primary actions are ink, never accent, by default.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Replaceable Brand Rule",
        "body": "Never hard-code the pink. Use the accent, tint and ring tokens, so a Partner's color reaches everything.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif Names, Sans Works Rule",
        "body": "The serif is for page titles, panel titles and headline figures. Labels, buttons, table cells and card headings are always sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Any number that sits in a column or changes in place uses tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sheets Don't Stack Rule",
        "body": "A card is never placed inside a card. Inside a sheet, divide with hairlines.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Border Or Shadow Rule",
        "body": "A resting surface gets a shadow, a control gets a border. A choice card keeps its border because the border shows what's selected.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do open every form in the side panel, with its actions in the panel footer.",
      "Do use ink for the primary action and keep the accent for rare emphasis.",
      "Do use the Sheet shadow for resting surfaces, and hairlines for division inside them.",
      "Do test every new screen with a non-pink accent and in dark mode.",
      "Do keep text at Faint Pencil or darker, and draw focus with Focus Pink.",
      "Do reuse the shared navigation row, fields and buttons rather than restyling them on a page.",
      "Do keep the ink-to-brand sheen for a single word in a headline. It is the one sanctioned gradient on text."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't open a form in a centered dialog. Forms belong in the side panel.",
      "Don't hard-code the pink or any brand color.",
      "Don't put a border on a resting card, or a card inside a card.",
      "Don't set labels, buttons, table cells or card headings in the serif.",
      "Don't give a button the Sheet shadow.",
      "Don't replace a native dropdown's open list with a custom menu.",
      "Don't let the page grid or glow run behind working content."
    ]
  }
}
